# Project Overview

| Item | Value |
|---|---|
| **Name** | rs-game-dev |
| **Summary** | A Rust adventure game engine with a visual-novel core and plugin-based minigames (2D/3D action, RPG, puzzle, RTS). |
| **Language** | Rust |
| **Build Tool** | Cargo (workspace) |
| **References** | Koihime Musou, TWINKLE CRUSADERS |

## Tech Stack

| Category | Technology |
|---|---|
| **Renderer** | Google Filament (PBR, IBL, post-processing) |
| **2D Characters** | Live2D Cubism Native SDK (C++ -> Rust FFI) |
| **3D Characters** | VRM / FBX (SpringBone, BlendShape, GLB conversion) |
| **UI Layout** | Taffy (Flexbox) + signal-driven reactivity (Floem-inspired) |
| **UI Rendering** | SDF text, Glassmorphism materials |
| **Audio** | `kira` or `rodio` (BGM/SE/Voice mixing) |
| **ECS** | Custom Entity Component System |
| **Serialization** | `serde`, `rmp-serde` (MessagePack), CSV metadata |
| **Script** | Tag-based custom script syntax (parser + state machine) |
| **RNG** | Xoshiro256++ (visual effects) / ChaCha8 (logic/replay) |

## Core Principles

- Respect Rust memory safety and borrowing rules; restrict `unsafe` to FFI boundaries.
- Always enforce `clippy` and `rustfmt`.
- Keep ECS and UI loosely coupled via message passing, not direct references.
- Add minigames as independent plugins implementing the `Scene` trait.
- Store save data in MessagePack format (`rmp-serde`).
